    title: 'The Trans-Atlantic Slave Trade: Stories History Books Left Out',
    excerpt: 'The standard account frames the enslaved as passive sufferers of an overwhelming historical crime. What it erases is extraordinary: the resistance, the rebellion, the cultural preservation, and the ongoing assertion of human dignity against a system designed to annihilate it.',
