    excerpt: 'The distinction between scarcity and abundance thinking sounds like motivational-poster language. Beneath it lies a claim about human cognition that is well-supported by behavioural science — and a parallel claim about consciousness that draws on wisdom traditions from every inhabited continent.',
    author: 'J.N. Nartey',
